  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to improve the understanding of the status of N. concolor in Nam Kan NPA, to support management planning and prioritize resources for the conservation of the species. This will be done by: 1) providing the necessary training to local government and NGO staff and then carrying out field surveys of the gibbons to complete the picture of the status and distribution of gibbons throughout the entire NPA; 2) assessing threats to gibbons through village interviews; 3) conducting a village awareness program; 4) engaging stakeholders where targeted responses are needed to address threats; 5) using all opportunities to engage with relevant stakeholders through informal consultations, arranged meetings, and a series of workshops and village meetings to prepare a Species Conservation Action Plan; 6) facilitating the implementation of effective law enforcement patrols through provision of SMART training to the village law enforcement patrol teams; and 7) engaging with relevant stakeholders to socialize issues relating to provincial boundary demarcation so that a workable solution may be found that removes the hindrance caused by the ambiguity of the boundary location that is hindering conservation and management of the NPA.</narrative>
  </description>
